 ntbrite at letsglowfestival.eventb\nPrice: Free\nCategories: community\, f
 ree\nSource: funcheap/san-jose+funcheap/south-bay\n\nBART’s Let’s Glow
 ! BART Anime Festival returns to Warm Springs/South Fremont Station for a 
 celebration of anime\, art\, music\, cosplay and transit fandom. This year
 ’s free festival will be bigger and better than ever\, following a huge 
 turnout of more than 4\,000 attendees last year! The festival celebrates t
 he shared fandom of anime and transit\, with an expanded lineup of artists
 \, performances\, food\, cosplay\, and more. Get to know BART’s anime ma
 scots at bart.gov/anime . Details What: Let’s Glow! BART Anime Festival 
 When: Saturday\, September 19\, 4pm to 9pm Where: Warm Springs/South Fremo
 nt Station RSVP on Eventbrite at letsglowfestival.eventbrite.com . Not req
 uired but helps us get a headcount. Free to attend What to expect Artist A
 lley: More than 100 artists will sell a mix of BART\, anime-\, and transit
 -themed art\, along with their own original artwork. Check back for the fu
 ll catalog in the coming weeks. Music and performances: AniClover will DJ 
 all night\, and SanFlare will perform wotagei\, a high-energy style of syn
 chronized fan dancing. SanFlare will also teach attendees the official BAR
 T wotagei dance. Special Youtaite concert: An exclusive VTuber concert pro
 duced by Neon Shrine f
LOCATION:Warm Springs/South Fremont Station RSVP on Eventbrite at letsglow
